-- title:
--   Functions regular off the ends are finitely generated (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime together with the hypothesis $hq2 : q = 2$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$; in addition an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ is fixed. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $\kappa := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$.
--
--   The first block of data concerns level $M'$ over $\kappa$. Here `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((Q))$ generated by the two Laurent series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`. A finite set $W$ of places of this field over $\kappa$ is given, and the hypothesis `hW` states that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, of those places $w$ which are rational (the structural map $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), are affine geometric places, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ M')$ lies in the supersingular set `ssJSet q κ`; a member $s$ of $W$ is singled out.
--
--   The second block concerns the characteristic-zero function fields. `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$, of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a place map of the same degrees, compatibility of the contraction of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $A$ and of the residue map with $A \to \kappa$, the scaling property that every nonzero element becomes an integral element with nonzero residue after multiplication by a suitable constant, and the compatibility of divisors with the place map. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, viewed in $\kappa((Q))$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to \kappa$.
--
--   The third block is the prolongation to the full level and its chart data. $F_{SS}$ is a field and a $\kappa$-algebra; $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{SS}$, that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of `fieldBar q M'` with a surjective residue map onto $F_{SS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, and satisfying the same scaling property. Furthermore $N$ is a finite set of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$, and for each place $Q$ of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$ there are given a subring $S_x Q$ of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_x Q : A[X] \to S_x Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{0x} Q : S_x Q \to \kappa$, and a set $D_x Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are the following. `h0`: some element of $F_{SS}$ is transcendental over $\kappa$. `h1` (compatibility of $R$ with $R_0$ at $s$): for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image under $\kappa \to F_{SS}$ of the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$. `h2`: for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the contraction of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equals $R.\mathrm{integers}$. `hcard`: $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   `hpkg` (the smooth-point package, fourteen clauses, summarised here) requires, for every place $Q \notin N$: the image of $A$ lies in $S_x Q$; $\varphi_x Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_x Q$ sends a constant $C a$ to the image of $a$, and $\chi_{0x} Q$ sends it to the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$, while $\chi_{0x} Q (\varphi_x Q X) = 0$; for every $c \in A$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $S_x Q \to A$ splitting the constants, lifting $\chi_{0x} Q$ and sending $\varphi_x Q X$ to $c$; every $f \in S_x Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_{0x} Q f$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_x Q X$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_x Q$ consists precisely of the rational places $P$ such that every $f \in S_x Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f \in A$, and such that $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f$ is $<1$ exactly when $\chi_{0x} Q f = 0$; every homomorphism $S_x Q \to A$ splitting the constants and lifting $\chi_{0x} Q$ is realised by a unique place in $D_x Q$ via $\mathrm{evalAt}$; for $P \in D_x Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_x Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h \ne 0$; every nonzero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f = 0$ for all $P \in D_x Q$ becomes, after multiplication by the image of a nonzero constant of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a unit of $S_x Q$; and every $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_x Q$ lies in $S_x Q$.
--
--   `hdisj`: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some place lies in both $D_x Q$ and $D_x Q'$ then $Q = Q'$. `hcusp`: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_x Q$, the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $q$-expansion `jq` has nonnegative order at $P$. `heqv`: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}(\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M')$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and for every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced $\kappa$-automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ of $F_{SS}$ preserves $N$ (membership in $N$ is invariant), and for $Q \notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dx Q) = Dx (R.resAut τ hτ • Q)`. `hUniq` (uniqueness of the package): for $Q \notin N$, any quadruple $(S, \varphi, \chi_0, D)$ satisfying the same fourteen clauses satisfies $D = D_x Q$, $S = S_x Q$, and $\chi_0$ agrees with $\chi_{0x} Q$ on common elements.
--
--   `hdl` (the Drinfeld identification) assumes: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $F_{SS}$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C_s`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field (the fraction field of the coordinate ring) of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$, such that the cardinality of $C_s$ equals `placeWidthChar q M' s` — namely `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$, which for $q = 2$ is $12$ if that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` — and such that $e$ is equivariant: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in `hSubgroup q` (the kernel of the character $(g,u) \mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb Z/q) \times \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$), the image under $e$ of $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1})$ applied to any $x \in F_{SS}$ coincides, inside the Drinfeld function field, with the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ via [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) on the image of $x$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a natural number $n$ and a family $z : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to F_{SS}$ such that: first, each $z_i$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $Q$ of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$ with $Q \notin N$; and second, every $f \in F_{SS}$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q \notin N$ belongs to the $\kappa$-subalgebra of $F_{SS}$ generated by the range of $z$. Thus the functions on $F_{SS}$ regular away from the $q+1$ ends $N$ are contained in a $\kappa$-algebra generated by finitely many such functions.
--
--   This is the finite-generation statement for the ring of functions on the supersingular reduced fibre which are regular away from the $q+1$ distinguished places (the ends), in the case $q = 2$ at a rigidified auxiliary level given by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$; the reduced fibre is identified through `hdl` with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd), in the construction of affine charts for the semistable model of the modular curve at $q$.
